{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"fruited-fragrant-kitty","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe user-level Copilot skills `rebar-implement`, `rebar-janitor`, and `rebar-debug`\n(symlinked into `~/.copilot/skills/` from `examples/agent-skills/`) silently fail to\nregister in GitHub Copilot CLI, while `rebar-brainstorm` registers fine. Copilot CLI\nenforces the Agent Skills spec's 1024-character `description` cap and a strict YAML\nfrontmatter parse, but drops non-conforming skills silently — no error, no warning\n(github/copilot-cli#3494; YAML strictness in #1024). The three failing skills each hit a\ntrigger: `rebar-implement` (1327-char description) and `rebar-janitor` (1068-char) exceed\n1024; `rebar-debug` (868-char) contains an unquoted `: ` (`discipline: write`) that breaks\nthe YAML plain scalar. Nothing in the repo guards against this regressing.\n\n## Approach\n\nTwo parts. (1) Fix the three `SKILL.md` frontmatters: rewrite each `description` as a YAML\nfolded block scalar (`description: >-`), matching the packaged builtin skills' style, which\nneutralizes colon/quote parse breaks, and trim the two over-cap descriptions to <= 1024\ncharacters while preserving each skill's \"Use when … or invokes /rebar-<name>\" trigger.\n(2) Add a deterministic CI lint that fails when any tracked `SKILL.md` has invalid\nfrontmatter — following the established `scripts/check_*.py` + `make lint` convention\n(e.g. `scripts/check_docs_index.py` wired at `Makefile:185`, mirrored by\n`tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py`). This fits because it single-sources the rule the\nsame way existing structural gates do, and catches the failure class at commit/CI time\ninstead of silently at skill-load time.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-implement/SKILL.md` — block-scalar + trim description to <=1024.\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-janitor/SKILL.md` — block-scalar + trim description to <=1024.\n- `examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md` — block-scalar to fix the unquoted `: `.\n- `scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` — new lint: for every `examples/agent-skills/*/SKILL.md`,\n  assert the frontmatter parses as YAML, `description` is present, non-empty, and <= 1024\n  characters, and `name` (when present) is <= 64 chars and matches `^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$`.\n  Expose importable `check_file`/`main(argv)->int` returning exit code, printing findings.\n- `tests/unit/test_check_skill_frontmatter.py` — new test mirroring the check-script pattern\n  (importlib-loaded, `pytest.mark.unit`): the real tree passes; synthetic over-cap,\n  empty-description, unparseable-YAML, and bad-name fixtures each fail.\n- `Makefile` — invoke `python scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` from the `lint` target.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Happy path: `python scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` exits 0 on the committed tree\n  (all four skills valid after the fix); the unit test asserts this via `chk.main([]) == 0`.\n- Failure/edge paths (unit test, synthetic fixtures): a 1200-char description fails; an\n  empty description fails; frontmatter with an unquoted `: ` that yields non-string/parse\n  error fails; a `name` over 64 chars or violating the regex fails.\n- Regression check: assert each real skill's parsed description length is <= 1024 and each\n  file's frontmatter YAML-parses to a mapping with a string `description`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All four `examples/agent-skills/*/SKILL.md` frontmatters parse as YAML to a mapping\n      whose `description` is a non-empty string <= 1024 chars — verified by\n      `python scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` exiting 0.\n- [ ] `rebar-implement`, `rebar-janitor`, and `rebar-debug` descriptions each still contain\n      their `/rebar-<name>` invocation trigger — verified by grep in the unit test.\n- [ ] `scripts/check_skill_frontmatter.py` exists and, run standalone, exits non-zero with a\n      clear message when given a fixture SKILL.md whose description exceeds 1024 chars —\n      verified by the unit test's failure cases.\n- [ ] `make lint` invokes the new check — verified by grepping the `lint` target for\n      `check_skill_frontmatter` and by `make lint` passing on the fixed tree.\n- [ ] The unit test `tests/unit/test_check_skill_frontmatter.py` passes under\n      `pytest -m unit` (happy path + over-cap + empty + unparseable + bad-name cases).","id":"1fa8-ebe0-8cca-4d89","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Fix silently-dropped Copilot rebar skills and add a SKILL.md frontmatter lint"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786119053973247001,"uuid":"b8ff12b8-e89c-45c1-bc0b-504aaf96b802"}